                              "Add a new clause 2.13.1 as follows:",
                              "\u201cThe Sub-Contractor has inspected the physical and other site conditions (conditions as would be discoverable upon inspection as at the date of this Sub-Contract and other conditions external to but affecting the Site including the land and structures adjacent to the Site, to the extent they relate to the Sub-Contract Works and/or are likely to affect the manner in which the Sub-Contract Works may be performed and has fully acquainted himself with the same and has reviewed all information issued to him as to risks, contingencies and related circumstances which may influence or affect the carrying out and completion of the Sub-Contract Works, including the means of access and facilities for storage and delivery of plant, materials and Sub-Contractor\u2019s equipment. No failure on the part of the Sub-Contractor to discover, review or foresee any such conditions, to the extent that they were issued for review, reasonably discoverable or foreseeable, shall entitle the Sub-Contractor to an adjustment to the Sub-Contract Sum or to an extension of time. Subject to clause 2.10, the Sub-Contractor shall be entitled to rely upon any survey, report or other document prepared by or on behalf of the Contractor and which forms part of this Sub-Contract regarding any such matter as is referred to in this clause as to the accuracy of any such survey, report or document or for any representation or statement contained therein, whether made negligently or otherwise save where the Sub-Contractor\u2019s obligations of performance under this Sub-Contract include a requirement to consider and/or verify the accuracy or completeness of and/or to identify any relevant discrepancies within or between any such survey, report or document.\u201d"
